  "notes": "Bench2Drive 220-route sweep, 6-8 Nov 2026, one RTX PRO 6000 (shared), CARLA 0.9.15, Bench2Drive 7ec25d1 + patches 0001-0002; per_route_timeout_s 5400, no early stop, up to 3 attempts per route (a run that broke in the simulator or the client was set aside and the route driven again). Routes 11715, 11755 were driven with patch 0003 as well (the ActorFlow far-car guard), because without it CARLA crashed on them (signal 11, large-map dormancy of a flow car with a collision sensor); the guard acted on none of them (`ActorFlow: removed flow car` in evaluator.log) and changes nothing on a route where it does not act. Asked at 2 Hz and handed a frame every 0.1 s between plans (POST /observe), the setting PR #167 declares; the sweep set it on the host (PADDOCK_OBSERVE_HZ=10), before runs recorded it. 22 of 22 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to qwendrive on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 22/22 source runs recorded. PADDOCK_OBSERVE_HZ was supplied by the ingest config and recorded by no source run, so it is the operator's assertion about the campaign, not a reading from it. asked for a plan at 2 Hz, the planning_hz the model's model.yaml declared for these runs, the last plan followed in between.",
